&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join the Customer Advocacy and Programs team, a small, high-impact team inside Customer Success that amplifies the voice of the customer and turns feedback into measurable change. We synthesize customer input and frontline insights to surface the highest-value opportunities, then partner with Product, GTM, Support, Operations, and technical teams to turn those opportunities into durable tools, programs, and improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to help Stripe’s user-facing teams deliver more strategic, effective, and scalable experiences for users. We build the capabilities that help Customer Success Managers and the broader field better understand users, identify opportunities, and deliver value, while extending Customer Success impact beyond named coverage. We are establishing a more unified approach to Customer Success tooling and efficiency, with product discipline from problem discovery through adoption and measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Program Manager, Customer Success Efficiency and Scale, you will act as the product leader for a portfolio of internal tools, AI-enabled workflows, assets, and scaled programs that enable Customer Success and other user-facing teams. You’ll turn frontline pain points and user needs into a prioritized roadmap, define clear requirements and success measures, and partner with technical, data, and operational teams to deliver solutions that are adopted and create measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Although this role is titled Program Manager, it requires a strong product-management mindset and experience: deep user discovery, strategic prioritization, crisp product requirements, cross-functional delivery, and continuous iteration based on adoption and outcomes. You’ll operate in a highly ambiguous environment, create clarity across a broad stakeholder set, and balance near-term improvements with a longer-term vision for scaling Customer Success capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the roadmap:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Set and prioritize the Customer Success Efficiency and Scale roadmap, balancing user needs, business impact, feasibility, and organizational priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Discover and define problems: &lt;/strong&gt;Partner with Customer Success Managers, Sales, and other user-facing teams to identify pain points, validate opportunities, and determine where tooling, automation, AI, or self-service can create leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shape solutions: &lt;/strong&gt;Translate validated needs into clear product briefs, requirements, success metrics, and launch plans. Partner with technical teams to deliver scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive delivery and adoption:&lt;/strong&gt; Coordinate cross-functional execution, manage dependencies and trade-offs, and ensure each launch has a clear enablement, measurement, and iteration plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scale Customer Success (CS) impact: &lt;/strong&gt;Build tools, assets, and programmatic motions that help Sales and other teams deliver CS-caliber value where dedicated CSM coverage is not available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in product management, program management with substantial product ownership, business operations, consulting, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading products, platforms, workflows, or customer-facing solutions from discovery and prioritization through launch, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense and user empathy, with the ability to turn ambiguous qualitative and quantitative inputs into clear strategy and requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex, cross-functional work across technical, operational, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and structured problem-solving skills, including the ability to evaluate trade-offs and design scalable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and influence skills, with the ability to create clarity and drive alignment across frontline teams and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of comfort with AI tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal tools, automation, AI-enabled workflows, or self-service experiences for customer-facing or go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering, data, analytics, or AI teams to scope and deliver technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing multi-quarter roadmaps that balance quick wins with longer-term foundational investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Apps connect Stripe with the tools businesses already use, bringing relevant data and workflows into the Stripe Dashboard and third-party systems. The Strategic Apps team owns a portfolio of integrations with enterprise systems that are critical to our users’ workflows—from quote-to-cash and support to reporting. We help users embed Stripe more deeply into the way they run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Staff Product Manager to set the strategy and lead execution for Strategic Apps. You will own a portfolio of existing and new integrations, including those with systems such as Salesforce, and determine where Stripe should invest based on user needs, Stripe’s product and industry priorities, and market signals. You will work across Stripe and directly with external partners to deliver reliable, high-quality integrations that drive adoption and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, product strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for a portfolio of strategic apps, making and communicating clear trade-offs amid significant ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and validate the highest-value user problems and integration opportunities through direct user research, ecosystem analysis, and quantitative evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Engineering, Design, Data Science, Finance, Sales, User Support, Marketing, Partner Management, and other product teams to deliver and evolve integrations end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to define product requirements, technical approach, and quality standards for integrations, including APIs, documentation, edge cases, reliability, security, compliance, and ongoing maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish feedback loops and measurement plans before launch; use product, business, and user metrics to assess efficacy, diagnose changes in performance, and continuously improve adoption, retention, and revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe’s product strategy with strategic technology partners and enterprise users, building productive relationships with product and technical counterparts and incorporating their feedback into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive launches, beta programs, user acceptance testing, and go-to-market readiness in partnership with Marketing, Sales, Partner Management, and Support; ensure teams have the materials and operating model needed to support adoption at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make and drive important cross-functional decisions, align senior stakeholders around a shared strategy, and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance new feature development with investment in quality, reliability, technical debt, and foundational platform capabilities across the app portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how Stripe builds and operates strategic integrations by turning user, partner, and performance signals into scalable product and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant product-management, engineering, or equivalent experience, including ownership of a high-quality product or feature area at scale or a major evolution of an existing product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting product strategy and driving execution across multiple cross-functional teams or a complex product area, from ambiguous problem definition through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use qualitative and quantitative evidence to define success metrics, evaluate product performance, and make prioritization decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and fluency working with engineers on API-based products, integrations, technical constraints, and product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging directly with enterprise users and external technology partners, and translating their needs into clear product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of influencing senior stakeholders and leading through organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise business systems and workflows, such as CRM, ERP, quote-to-cash, support, or reporting platforms; familiarity with Salesforce, Oracle, SAP, or Microsoft Dynamics is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling platform, ecosystem, marketplace, or partner-integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing product adoption, usage, or revenue through product-led and go-to-market initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or other regulated technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, engineering, or another technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Klaviyo’s platform is built on a foundation of secure, scalable account and identity systems that power every customer interaction. As we continue to grow into more complex enterprise use cases and regulated environments, the importance of account integrity, abuse prevention, and flexible organization modeling is critical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of Platform Integrity &amp;amp; Protection area (PAA) and the Accounts teams, partnering closely with Identity &amp;amp; Access Management (IAM), Security, Compliance, and Core Platform teams. Together, these teams define how accounts are created, structured, secured, and governed across Klaviyo. &lt;strong&gt;Please note this role requires 5 &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;days/week in our Boston office.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Senior Product Manager to own the end-to-end strategy across Platform Integrity &amp;amp; Protection (PAA) and Accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, cross-functional role responsible for shaping how Klaviyo:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protects customer accounts and prevents abuse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Models accounts and organizations at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports enterprise, compliance, and multi-entity use cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds platform tools that unlock self-serve capabilities and scalable workflows for stakeholders across the entire business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will serve as the single-threaded product owner across these domains, ensuring that decisions around security, identity, and account structure are made cohesively, not in silos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make a Difference&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive product strategy and roadmap across Platform Integrity &amp;amp; Protection and Accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve Klaviyo’s account and organization model to support enterprise scale and complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives focused on account security, authentication abuse prevention, and risk mitigation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with IAM to align authentication, authorization, and identity systems with account modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Security, Compliance, Legal, and GTM teams to meet regulatory and enterprise requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align multiple engineering teams around shared data models, platform capabilities, and security posture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track metrics for account security, abuse prevention, and platform health&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable other product teams by building shared frameworks (e.g., permissions, lifecycle hooks, settings systems)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clarity and alignment across stakeholders on tradeoffs between security, usability, and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Work On&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building a unified account model that supports multi-brand, multi-entity customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing a scalable anti-abuse platform with consistent enforcement across channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving account lifecycle management, from creation through closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthening platform security and risk detection capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reducing friction for customers and internal teams through clearer account and org experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 5+ years of product management experience, ideally in platform, infrastructure, or security domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience working on account systems, identity, permissions, or data models in B2B SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable operating in technical problem spaces and partnering closely with engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience driving cross-team alignment and influencing without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can balance short-term execution with long-term platform strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable navigating ambiguity and defining structure in complex environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly and can articulate tradeoffs to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with identity and access management (IAM) systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with security, compliance, or abuse prevention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise or regulated environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform APIs or shared services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring PMs or leading cross-functional initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Massachusetts Applicants:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;It is unlawful in Massachusetts to require or administer a lie detector test as a condition of employment or continued employment. An employer who violates this law shall be subject to criminal penalties and civil liability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our salary range reflects the cost of labor across various U.S. geographic markets. The range displayed below reflects the minimum and maximum target salaries for the position across all our US locations. The base salary offered for this position is determined by several factors, including the applicant’s job-related skills, relevant experience, education or training, and work location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to base salary, our total compensation package may include participation in the company’s annual cash bonus plan, variable compensation (OTE) for sales and customer success roles, equity, sign-on payments, and a comprehensive range of health, welfare, and wellbeing benefits based on eligibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your recruiter can provide more details about the specific salary/OTE range for your preferred location during the hiring process.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Base Pay Range For US Locations:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$136,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$204,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role may require up to 10% travel for purposes such as new hire onboarding, client or partner work if applicable, team meetings, and industry events. Travel is coordinated in advance.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Get to Know Klaviyo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re Klaviyo (pronounced clay-vee-oh). We empower creators to own their destiny by making first-party data accessible and actionable like never before. We see limitless potential for the technology we’re developing to nurture personalized experiences in ecommerce and beyond. To reach our goals, we need our own crew of remarkable creators—ambitious and collaborative teammates who stay focused on our north star: delighting our customers. If you’re ready to do the best work of your career, where you’ll be welcomed as your whole self from day one and supported with generous benefits, we hope you’ll join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;AI fluency at Klaviyo includes responsible use of AI (including privacy, security, bias awareness, and human-in-the-loop). We provide accommodations as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By participating in Klaviyo’s interview process, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and will adhere to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/careers/ai-guidance&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.klaviyo.com/careers/ai-guidance&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1761072778777000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw0auUcRqeYRczM9UoXAKldj&quot;&gt;Guidelines for using AI in the Klaviyo interview Process&lt;/a&gt;. For more information about how we process your personal data, see our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.klaviyo.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.klaviyo.com/legal/job-applicant-privacy-notice&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1761072778777000&amp;amp;usg=AOvVaw1axMoReIM1qwTbmaPcLI_b&quot;&gt;Job Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Klaviyo is committed to a policy of equal opportunity and non-discrimination. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, ethnicity, citizenship, national origin, color, religion or religious creed, age, sex (including pregnancy), gender identity, sexual orientation, physical or mental disability, veteran or active military status, marital status, criminal record, genetics, retaliation, sexual harassment or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
